**Recommendation: Redis Streams.** At your projected peak (~50–450 msg/s, worst case ~1.5k/s) you are 1–2 orders of magnitude below single-node `XADD` capacity even at 10x growth, and Redis is already an operated component. The decisive factors are the constraints: no infra engineer, zero Kafka experience, 2-week budget, and modest spend — Kafka's throughput and EOS advantages don't apply at this scale, and its EOS doesn't even cover external email/webhook side effects (verified: Confluent docs state Kafka transactions can't include external systems), so exactly-once for billing is an idempotency-table problem either way. Kafka's real wins (disk durability, long replay, keyed ordering) are documented as revisit triggers at ~100x volume.
